THE AI-NATIVE PATENT INSTITUTION (AIPI)

Redesigning Intellectual Property Governance for an Era of Abundant Machine Intelligence

Author: ouadi Maakoul 

AI : chatGpt, Claude 

June 2026


ABSTRACT
The global patent system, forged in an age of scarce invention, is collapsing under the Inventive Flood of AI-generated knowledge. This dissertation restates the AI-Native Patent Institution (AIPI) as a complete, adversarial-resilient framework. Four refined pillars—an enriched Global Knowledge Graph, a Multi-Dimensional Evaluation Protocol, a Verified Contribution Stratification Doctrine, and an Adaptive Protection Calculus—are integrated with a new adversarial analysis chapter, real economic incentives for the Innovation Commons, and a politically calibrated Public Benefit Test. Human sovereignty is preserved as a constitutional necessity, grounded in a non-automability theorem. The architecture ensures that AI-driven abundance is not captured as monopoly rent but steered toward inclusive civilizational progress.

