CHAPTER 6: VERIFIED CONTRIBUTION STRATIFICATION DOCTRINE (VCSD)

The original CSD’s self-reported $\lambda$ was its greatest vulnerability. The VCSD replaces it with a cryptographically verifiable metric, transforming the doctrine into an incentive-compatible audit system.

Invention Session Ledger (ISL). Every AI-assisted inventive session must be recorded in an immutable, append-only ledger signed by all participating systems and human inventors. The ledger captures:

· Timestamped prompts and structured problem specifications.
· AI-generated intermediate outputs and their provenance.
· Human selection actions, validation steps, and iterative refinements.
· A machine-readable, standardised format enabling automated parsing.

Definition 6.1 (Verified λ_v).
\lambda_v(I) = \frac{H_{conc}^{audit} + H_{sel}^{audit} + H_{val}^{audit}}{H_{conc}^{audit} + H_{sel}^{audit} + H_{val}^{audit} + A_{gen}^{audit} + A_{opt}^{audit}}

The superscript “audit” indicates that each term is computed by a neutral protocol engine from the ISL, not by the applicant. $H_{conc}^{audit}$ is the effective human effort in problem conceptualisation, measured by structured prompt complexity and iterative refinement; $A_{gen}^{audit}$ is the volume of AI autonomous generation, weighted by self-reported system confidence.

Tier System (unchanged thresholds):

· Tier I ($\lambda_v \ge 0.7$): Standard patent, minimal extra disclosure, full term.
· Tier II ($0.4 \le \lambda_v < 0.7$): Reduced term (APC factor $\beta_{II}$), mandatory disclosure of AI model identity and training data provenance.
· Tier III ($0.1 \le \lambda_v < 0.4$): Must pass a mandatory Public Benefit Test; automatic co-registration of foundational claims in the Innovation Commons; term further reduced ($\beta_{III}$); FRAND licensing obligations.
· Tier IV ($\lambda_v < 0.1$): Deemed autonomous; no patent but entered in the Autonomous Disclosure Registry with a defensive shield.

Incentive compatibility: Applicants have no incentive to understate AI contribution because the ledger is audited; any discrepancy between declared and audited $\lambda_v$ triggers patent invalidation and financial penalties. Moreover, examination fees rise with AI contribution fraction, discouraging AI-dominant flooding. The system rewards transparent, verifiable human creativity.

Disclosure obligations: All tiers must register the AI systems used; Tier III and IV inventions must publish the generation methodology. Fraudulent disclosure constitutes material fraud and is actionable.

