APPENDIX D: MULTI-DIMENSIONAL EVALUATION PROTOCOL — DETAILED INDEX FORMULAE

D.1 Utility Index (UI)

$UI(I) = \frac{1}{|D|} \sum_{d \in D} \text{Rel}(I,d) \times \text{Imp}(I,d)$

· $D$: set of application domains (from GKG domain taxonomy).
· $\text{Rel}(I,d)$: Probability that $I$ applies to domain $d$, estimated via a supervised classifier trained on patent-domain assignments.
· $\text{Imp}(I,d)$: Expected utility improvement over current practice. Computed as the predicted performance gain (from technical claims) weighted by domain importance (e.g., disease burden, market size). A domain-specific benchmark database provides baseline performance metrics.

D.2 Reproducibility Index (RI)

$RI(I) = \prod_{c \in claims} \text{coverage}(c, spec) \times \text{experimental\_evidence\_score}$

· $\text{coverage}(c, spec)$: Fraction of claim elements that are explicitly enabled in the specification, using an NLP entailment model.
· $\text{experimental\_evidence\_score}$: Based on presence of working examples, validated against independent replication database. For high-priority applications, an independent lab may attempt reproduction (cost charged to applicant).

D.3 Impact Index (II)

$II(I) = w_1 \hat{C}(I) + w_2 \hat{M}(I) + w_3 \hat{B}(I)$

· $\hat{C}(I)$: Predicted forward citation count at 5 years, from a graph neural network trained on GKG citation dynamics.
· $\hat{M}(I)$: Market impact estimate from a sector-specific economic model.
· $\hat{B}(I)$: Social benefit projection, using disability-adjusted life years (DALYs) averted for health, tonnes of CO2 reduced for climate, etc.

Uncertainty bound: $II(I) \pm \sigma_{II}$ from ensemble of models.

D.4 Risk Index (RSI)

$RSI(I) = 1 - \max_{r} P(harm_r | I)$

Where $P(harm_r)$ is estimated via a structured risk assessment matrix:

· Environmental: toxicity prediction, life-cycle assessment model.
· Security: dual-use potential classification based on technology watch lists.
· Ethical: bias and surveillance risk assessed by an independent ethics panel using a checklist.
· Systemic: potential for cascading failures (e.g., financial algorithms).

Threshold $\tau_{RSI} = 0.3$ triggers extended review.

