APPENDIX F: PUBLIC BENEFIT TEST — MARKET CONCENTRATION METHODOLOGY

F.1 Market Definition and HHI Calculation

The relevant market is defined using the GKG’s technology classification system (a refined version of CPC/IPC) and applicant’s declared field of use. The pre-grant HHI is calculated from publicly available market share data (sales, licenses) of firms active in that field. The post-grant HHI assumes the patentee gains the full market share of the invention (if it replaces existing products) or adds to concentration.

$MC(I) = \max(0, HHI_{post} - HHI_{pre})$, capped at 0.1 to avoid domination of index.

F.2 Threshold $\tau_{PBT}$ Calibration

Initial $\tau_{PBT} = 0.4$ (on a scale where $UI, RSI \in [0,1]$). It is set such that an invention with neutral utility and low risk passes, but one with moderate utility but high concentration penalty might fail. The threshold is adjustable by the Policy Council with supermajority.

