APPENDIX G: ADVERSARIAL THREAT MODEL — FORMAL DEFINITIONS AND DETECTION ALGORITHMS

G.1 Threat Model Overview

· T1 – Flooding: Attacker files $N$ applications with minimal human contribution, hoping some pass.
· T2 – Embedding Manipulation: Attacker crafts claims to maximize $f_{dist}$ while keeping the invention trivial.
· T3 – Synthetic Prior Art: Attacker injects false documents $D_{fake}$ into GKG sources.
· T4 – Graph Poisoning: Attacker manipulates citations to increase edge weights toward attacker’s patents.
· T5 – Governance Capture: Attacker influences parameter setting.

G.2 Anti-Flooding Mechanism

Define Application Score $A(I) = NI_+(I) \times UI(I)$. Examiners automatically reject any application with $A(I) < \tau_{floor}$ without full review (administrative rejection). Fee schedule: $fee(N) = base \times N^\beta$ for $N$ applications from one entity per year, with $\beta = 1.5$. Large-scale flooding becomes economically irrational.

G.3 Embedding Manipulation Detector

We compute a Linguistic Obfuscation Score $LOS(I)$ measuring how much the claim text deviates from typical patent language in the same technical field, using perplexity under a field-specific language model. If $LOS > \tau_{lang}$, the application is flagged for enhanced human review. Additionally, the enriched $f_{causal}$ component naturally penalises trivial substitutions; an attacker who uses exotic wording but the same functional/causal structure will see low $NI_+$.

G.4 Synthetic Prior Art Detection (Algorithm)

Algorithm SPAD (Synthetic Prior Art Detector):

1. For each document $d$ newly ingested:
   a. Check provenance: must be from a registered, trusted repository (verified via digital signature).
   b. Compute outlier score on content embedding relative to its declared field: if it lies outside the 99% confidence interval of the field’s document distribution, flag.
   c. Temporal burst detection: if $> \sigma$ documents from a new source appear in a short window, quarantine all.
2. Flagged documents are sent to a human review panel. Confirmed synthetic documents result in permanent blacklisting of the submitting source and mandatory re-examination of any patent citing them.

G.5 Governance Capture Resistance

Key parameters (APC weights, MDEP thresholds, CSD tier boundaries) are defined in smart contracts on a public blockchain with a time-lock and multi-signature governance by the Policy Council. Any change must pass a 60-day public comment period and a separate adversarial review panel. The panel is composed of five independent academics selected by sortition from a global roster, with veto power if they find the change benefits a single firm or coalition disproportionately.

