APPENDIX H: INNOVATION COMMONS — ECONOMIC INCENTIVES DETAIL

H.1 Tax Credit Specification

An entity registering an invention $I$ in the Innovation Commons receives a tax credit equal to $c \times \text{Qualified R&D Expenses}$ attributed to the invention, where $c$ is set by national law (suggested 20%). The qualified expenses are verified by audit. The total credit per invention is capped at $2 million to prevent abuse.

H.2 Sovereign Innovation Fund (SIF)

The SIF is a multilateral fund contributed by member states. It allocates grants via a competitive process to entities that:

· Dedicate a portfolio of Commons-registered inventions in priority areas (pandemic preparedness, climate mitigation).
· The grant amount is proportional to the aggregate Impact Index of the portfolio.
· Special Fast-Track for small and medium enterprises.

H.3 ICS and Procurement Advantage

ICS is a cumulated score $ICS_{entity} = \sum_{I \in \text{commons}} II(I) \times RI(I)$. In public procurement tenders, bidding companies receive an evaluation bonus: a 5% price advantage for ICS above a threshold. This makes the Commons a strategic asset.

